From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:30:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vello_cpu: a render context takes at most 4 workers by
 default

The default was one worker per core but one, up to 8. Measured in
hotty-blitz (a 300-frame dashboard replay and its bench, on a Ryzen 5
5600X and a Ryzen AI laptop), 4 workers paint small partial frames
faster than 8 at about 35% less CPU, and a full 3.45 Mpx paint within
~5% of 8: past 2 workers it barely gets faster, the main thread's share
(scene, strips, dispatch) dominating. Each worker also adds dispatch and
idle spinning to every small paint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/render.rs | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/render.rs b/src/render.rs
index ecc8a87..68d33c6 100644
--- a/src/render.rs
+++ b/src/render.rs
@@ -192,12 +192,15 @@ impl Default for RenderSettings {
     fn default() -> Self {
         Self {
             level: Level::try_detect().unwrap_or(Level::baseline()),
+            // At most 4 workers: past 2, a full paint barely gets faster
+            // (the main thread's share dominates), while each worker adds
+            // dispatch and idle spinning to every small paint.
             #[cfg(feature = "multithreading")]
             num_threads: (std::thread::available_parallelism()
                 .unwrap()
                 .get()
                 .saturating_sub(1) as u16)
-                .min(8),
+                .min(4),
             #[cfg(not(feature = "multithreading"))]
             num_threads: 0,
         }
